=== RESUMED SUPERVISOR (2026-10-08T08:09Z) ===
Previous supervisor died with 3x S1 in flight. Recovered results:
- t6_trivium64 (19.8u/372): S1 KILLED — LIN FLAG rej=10/10 (D=4096/4096 logp=-inf), DIFF FLAG rej=10/10. Hard kill.
- t6_gimli (21.4u/4890): S1 KILLED — same catastrophic LIN/DIFF signature.
- t6_trivium64b (25.5u/1108): S1 still running (30 min in).

MECHANISTIC HYPOTHESIS: stream-cipher/NFSR round functions assume fixed key during operation; as a 64-bit keyed finalizer with (input,key) both varying, 6-8 clocks of mostly-linear state update cannot kill linear trails at 64-bit width. The "free wiring" latency insight is real; the nonlinearity is insufficient. This is a construction-class kill for shift-register-cascade-at-64-bit, NOT a parameter-tuning problem.

NEXT: batch 4 — permutation-only-diffusion mini-SPN (4-bit S-box + bit-permutation, no XOR-tree linear layer). Each round = S-box (~3.5u) + permute (0u) + key XOR; 5 rounds ≈ 20u target. Genuinely different axis from (a,b) XOR linear layers and chi-cascades.

